cmac-self-test: test the block cipher of a CMAC before using it

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 1, "Self-Test Modes"): "If a command requires use
of an untested algorithm or functional module, the TPM performs the test and
then completes the command actions."

TPM2_MAC and TPM2_MAC_Start with a SYMCIPHER key compute a CMAC with the
block cipher of the key (AES), but CryptCmacStart() does not test it (its
CMAC code uses the key schedule of the block cipher directly, which bypasses
the TEST() of CryptSymmetricEncrypt()), so a MAC is returned while AES is
still untested (it stays in the toDoList of TPM2_IncrementalSelfTest, and
TPM2_GetTestResult reports TPM_RC_NEEDS_TEST). The HMAC path tests its hash in
CryptHashStart(). The patch runs TPM_DO_SELF_TEST() on the block cipher in
CryptCmacStart(), as tpm-rs does when it starts a CMAC (Camellia has no test
vectors and needs no test).

diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/crypt/CryptCmac.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/crypt/CryptCmac.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/crypt/CryptCmac.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/crypt/CryptCmac.c
@@ -27,6 +27,11 @@
     //
     if(macAlg != TPM_ALG_CMAC)
         return 0;
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // the CMAC is computed with the block cipher of the key, so the block cipher
+    // is tested first if it is untested (Part 1 "Self-Test Modes"), as
+    // CryptHashStart() does for the hash of an HMAC.
+    TPM_DO_SELF_TEST(def->algorithm);
     // set up the encryption algorithm and parameters
     cState->symAlg      = def->algorithm;
     cState->keySizeBits = def->keyBits.sym;
